@host = http://localhost:4004

#####
#
# ProcessorService — local semantic search (@cap-js/ai)
#
# searchIncidents(phrase) ranks incidents by cosine similarity between the phrase and
# each incident's stored embedding (title + conversation messages), computed locally
# via an ONNX model on SQLite — no SAP AI Core needed.
#

### Search by phrase — inverter incidents should rank highest
GET {{host}}/odata/v4/processor/searchIncidents(phrase='inverter%20problem')
Authorization: Basic alice:wonderland

### Search by conversation-only wording (not in any title) — proves messages are embedded
GET {{host}}/odata/v4/processor/searchIncidents(phrase='loose%20battery%20connections')
Authorization: Basic alice:wonderland

### Unrelated phrase — expect low relevance across the board
GET {{host}}/odata/v4/processor/searchIncidents(phrase='holiday%20booking%20refund')
Authorization: Basic alice:wonderland

#####
#
# Multilingual — Japanese phrases (swap the embedding model)
#
# The default model (sentence-transformers/all-MiniLM-L6-v2) is English-only, so Japanese
# phrases collapse to noise: "solar panel broken" tops out at ~0.06 and "loose battery
# connections" even goes negative — the model has no real representation for these tokens.
#
# Fix = swap to a multilingual model. No code change (the Vector element has no fixed
# dimension). For the demo an env override is easiest:
#   CDS_REQUIRES_DB_EMBEDDING_MODEL=sentence-transformers/paraphrase-multilingual-MiniLM-L12-v2 cds watch
# or set it permanently: cds.requires.db.embedding.model in package.json.
# First time only, download the model:
#   npx @cap-js/ai install-model sentence-transformers/paraphrase-multilingual-MiniLM-L12-v2
# An in-memory redeploy re-runs the backfill and re-computes every stored embedding.
#
# With the multilingual model Japanese works: "solar panel broken" jumps from ~0.06 to
# ~0.76 — a clean #1, on par with native English. Cross-lingual scores read a little lower
# than same-language, so calibrate the relevance threshold per language. One phrasing stays
# hard even here — the katakana "インバーターの問題" — a model/tokenization limit, not a data one.
#

### ソーラーパネルが壊れた  ("solar panel broken") — English model ~0.06 (noise) → multilingual ~0.76
GET {{host}}/odata/v4/processor/searchIncidents(phrase='ソーラーパネルが壊れた')
Authorization: Basic alice:wonderland

### バッテリーの接続が緩い  ("loose battery connections") — negative on the English model; ranks the right topic on multilingual
GET {{host}}/odata/v4/processor/searchIncidents(phrase='バッテリーの接続が緩い')
Authorization: Basic alice:wonderland

### インバーターの問題  ("inverter problem") — the hard case: near-noise even on the multilingual model
GET {{host}}/odata/v4/processor/searchIncidents(phrase='インバーターの問題')
Authorization: Basic alice:wonderland

#####
#
# Live edit → embedding recompute
#
# Adding a conversation message rebuilds `summary` (title + messages) in one roundtrip,
# and the stored calculated `embedding` is recomputed automatically by the database.
#

@incident = 3a4ede72-244a-4f5f-8efa-b17e032d01ee

### Baseline: this incident is only a weak match for "battery pack dead"
GET {{host}}/odata/v4/processor/searchIncidents(phrase='dead%20battery%20pack')
Authorization: Basic alice:wonderland

### 1) Put the incident into draft edit
POST {{host}}/odata/v4/processor/Incidents(ID={{incident}},IsActiveEntity=true)/ProcessorService.draftEdit
Authorization: Basic alice:wonderland
Content-Type: application/json

{ "PreserveChanges": true }

### 2) Add a conversation message mentioning the battery pack
POST {{host}}/odata/v4/processor/Incidents(ID={{incident}},IsActiveEntity=false)/conversation
Authorization: Basic alice:wonderland
Content-Type: application/json

{ "message": "The battery pack seems completely dead" }

### 3) Activate the draft — triggers summarize() and re-embeds
POST {{host}}/odata/v4/processor/Incidents(ID={{incident}},IsActiveEntity=false)/ProcessorService.draftActivate
Authorization: Basic alice:wonderland
Content-Type: application/json

{}

### 4) Re-run the search — this incident should now rank #1
GET {{host}}/odata/v4/processor/searchIncidents(phrase='dead%20battery%20pack')
Authorization: Basic alice:wonderland
